1
00:02:04,044 --> 00:02:08,284
No living creature was hurt during
the production of this show.

2
00:02:09,104 --> 00:02:13,484
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

3
00:02:35,255 --> 00:02:36,865
Murderer!

4
00:05:09,920 --> 00:05:11,600
Goktug!

5
00:05:12,055 --> 00:05:13,515
Boran.

6
00:05:41,952 --> 00:05:44,092
Many valiant alps of ours...

7
00:05:46,410 --> 00:05:48,120
our Beys...

8
00:05:49,344 --> 00:05:51,214
were murdered...

9
00:05:53,123 --> 00:05:55,973
stabbing them in the back...

10
00:05:57,723 --> 00:05:59,123
How to charge them?

11
00:06:00,455 --> 00:06:04,625
The bloody-handed murderers
tried to kill our traditions...

12
00:06:05,747 --> 00:06:07,857
They tried to end us...

13
00:06:10,291 --> 00:06:13,721
What does our religion say,
Sheik Edebalı?

14
00:06:17,791 --> 00:06:21,461
As it is written in Bakarah surah,
Osman Bey...

15
00:06:23,820 --> 00:06:27,390
Retalition is good for us.

16
00:06:39,358 --> 00:06:40,968
Now...

17
00:06:43,262 --> 00:06:44,852
Before dying...

18
00:06:46,453 --> 00:06:48,853
What are your final words?

19
00:07:15,686 --> 00:07:19,846
I've come this land to finish...

20
00:07:21,170 --> 00:07:22,650
what my father Noyan...

21
00:07:23,355 --> 00:07:26,685
left unfinished.

22
00:07:28,609 --> 00:07:29,979
I came to...

23
00:07:31,260 --> 00:07:32,680
end...

24
00:07:34,532 --> 00:07:36,402
your generation.

25
00:07:38,086 --> 00:07:44,376
Now I am kneeling in front of Gokboru...

26
00:07:46,440 --> 00:07:49,210
who is from Khan Tengri.

27
00:07:55,861 --> 00:07:59,441
Do I kneel because I seek forgiveness?

28
00:08:01,475 --> 00:08:02,865
Never.

29
00:08:04,976 --> 00:08:10,586
I kneel because I respect Gokboru
who managed to...

30
00:08:11,951 --> 00:08:15,971
defeat many Noyans
supported by dark souls...

31
00:08:17,380 --> 00:08:22,000
and Genghis Khan's valiant wolves.

32
00:08:29,292 --> 00:08:33,362
When I first saw you...

33
00:08:34,780 --> 00:08:39,300
You told me that you were going to...

34
00:08:39,897 --> 00:08:44,027
rip me apart under the blue sky.

35
00:08:50,027 --> 00:08:52,577
Keep your promise, Gokboru.

36
00:08:55,019 --> 00:08:58,539
Geyhatu's Hunter Dog...

37
00:09:00,007 --> 00:09:02,167
Black Shaman Togay...

38
00:09:03,538 --> 00:09:05,078
You defeated him.

39
00:09:08,454 --> 00:09:13,724
You defeated me with your commitment...

40
00:09:15,037 --> 00:09:17,247
to your herd.

41
00:09:19,189 --> 00:09:25,109
Perform the justice of your generation,
the justice of...

42
00:09:31,208 --> 00:09:33,048
Khan Tengri...

43
00:09:33,807 --> 00:09:35,627
Osman Bey.

44
00:10:31,264 --> 00:10:33,184
Osman Bey!

45
00:10:33,184 --> 00:10:38,584
Victory goes to the ones whose swords are
sharpened with faith.

46
00:10:38,917 --> 00:10:42,917
Victory goes to the ones who fight
shoulder to shoulder...

47
00:10:43,646 --> 00:10:46,246
and move together.

48
00:11:18,105 --> 00:11:21,295
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim.
(In the name of Allah, the compassionate, the merciful)

49
00:11:23,642 --> 00:11:25,192
My Bey!

50
00:11:45,927 --> 00:11:49,947
The double swords my Bamsı Bey...

51
00:11:51,636 --> 00:11:53,506
gave to me.

52
00:11:58,690 --> 00:12:00,860
They have been waiting for this moment.

53
00:13:35,393 --> 00:13:40,533
I can't relieve no matter...

54
00:13:42,264 --> 00:13:46,054
what we do to them.

55
00:13:46,718 --> 00:13:50,618
My Osman, you shall live long.

56
00:13:51,155 --> 00:13:53,305
You shall live long.

57
00:14:06,093 --> 00:14:07,373
Dears!

58
00:14:08,426 --> 00:14:13,026
Today, we refresh ourselves.

59
00:14:13,184 --> 00:14:15,054
Those snakes thought that...

60
00:14:16,708 --> 00:14:20,538
we forget our pain and not chase
them.

61
00:14:21,487 --> 00:14:23,527
Those snakes thought that...

62
00:14:23,603 --> 00:14:26,213
we wouldn't take revenge...

63
00:14:28,001 --> 00:14:29,491
but...

64
00:14:30,995 --> 00:14:33,405
Dark Osman Bey...

65
00:14:34,335 --> 00:14:40,215
brought them to me with the
help of his paw like an eagle.

66
00:15:28,967 --> 00:15:30,787
Allah-u Akbar.
(Allah is the greatest.)

67
00:15:30,790 --> 00:15:32,790
Allah-u Akbar.
(Allah is the greatest.)

68
00:16:30,048 --> 00:16:32,818
Ertugrul Ghazi's son Osman Bey...

69
00:16:33,329 --> 00:16:38,069
gave everyone what they deserved...

70
00:16:38,217 --> 00:16:42,997
no matter what their religion is...

71
00:16:43,847 --> 00:16:48,017
what nationality they are.

72
00:16:58,614 --> 00:17:04,944
Our enemies can gather up and push us!

73
00:17:05,936 --> 00:17:11,316
They can push us with slyness,
with cruelty...

74
00:17:12,147 --> 00:17:15,047
They can try to stab us in the back.

75
00:17:15,680 --> 00:17:19,662
As long as our brotherhood remains...

76
00:17:19,662 --> 00:17:22,992
As long as my generation is there...

77
00:17:23,975 --> 00:17:30,605
Justice will always be performed
in this land.

78
00:17:35,074 --> 00:17:40,586
Neither Mongols nor Byzantine has
power to...

79
00:17:40,586 --> 00:17:43,416
undo what I say!

80
00:17:45,482 --> 00:17:48,102
May your justice be everlasting, Osman Bey

81
00:17:49,384 --> 00:18:03,211
Long live Osman Bey.

82
00:18:03,211 --> 00:18:34,301
Allah-u Akbar.
(Allah is the greatest.)

83
00:18:56,711 --> 00:19:00,961
Osman took Togay away from my hands!

84
00:19:02,876 --> 00:19:06,476
Togay is a rebel who disobeyed.

85
00:19:06,632 --> 00:19:08,952
Look at the bright side.

86
00:19:10,035 --> 00:19:13,205
Osman Bey saved you from a trouble.

87
00:19:13,725 --> 00:19:17,257
I should have made Togay pay.

88
00:19:17,257 --> 00:19:19,447
Not a Turk!

89
00:19:20,814 --> 00:19:23,414
Your soldiers dropped the ball...

90
00:19:23,469 --> 00:19:25,869
Osman Bey caught it.

91
00:19:26,070 --> 00:19:31,550
That he killed Togay saved both you and
me from a huge trouble. Accept it.

92
00:19:33,913 --> 00:19:41,209
Also, we have issues to take care of
before talking about Osman and Togay.

93
00:19:41,847 --> 00:19:46,547
Your taxes create uneasiness everywhere.

94
00:19:46,880 --> 00:19:51,350
The cruelty of your soldiers increase
the number of rebels.

95
00:19:51,819 --> 00:19:55,469
I won't let Osman go before
I punish him, Sultan Mesut.

96
00:19:57,926 --> 00:20:02,336
Does Osman Bey pay his taxes?
He does.

97
00:20:03,169 --> 00:20:06,829
Is he loyal to our agreement?
He is.

98
00:20:07,325 --> 00:20:10,585
If you chase vengeance...

99
00:20:11,226 --> 00:20:13,786
Taxes won't be the only thing you lose...

100
00:20:14,356 --> 00:20:17,796
You also draw Geyhatu's anger on you.

101
00:20:18,205 --> 00:20:20,235
It'll be my problem too.

102
00:20:20,333 --> 00:20:25,063
I don't want to draw Geyhatu's
anger on me.

103
00:20:25,458 --> 00:20:28,878
Osman will pay a price...

104
00:20:29,173 --> 00:20:34,103
But not with blood, with gold instead.

105
00:20:36,436 --> 00:20:38,099
What do you think?

106
00:20:38,099 --> 00:20:42,411
The price for taking Togay away from me...

107
00:20:42,411 --> 00:20:45,911
costs him a tax of three years.

108
00:20:47,709 --> 00:20:50,299
Isn't this too much?

109
00:20:50,864 --> 00:20:54,898
Disorder will take place in Bıtinya...

110
00:20:54,898 --> 00:20:57,578
if you try to ruin them.

111
00:20:58,447 --> 00:21:02,917
Also, are you sure that Osman
was the one...

112
00:21:03,246 --> 00:21:04,866
who took Togay?

113
00:21:11,773 --> 00:21:17,303
Are you kidding me, Sultan Mesut?

114
00:21:17,704 --> 00:21:24,930
I am not stupid enough to believe that
Osman didn't do this.

115
00:21:25,994 --> 00:21:27,784
You don't have a proof.

116
00:21:28,169 --> 00:21:33,019
I don't think Osman Bey and the other Beys
deserve this tax.

117
00:21:34,059 --> 00:21:38,589
I don't care about what you think.

118
00:21:39,025 --> 00:21:45,725
I'll have a stableman to tame a horse
like Osman.

119
00:21:53,199 --> 00:21:54,949
What does this mean?

120
00:21:54,952 --> 00:21:58,882
Nicola agaisnt Osman.

121
00:21:59,085 --> 00:22:04,505
I'll have Nicola as my man.

122
00:22:04,934 --> 00:22:09,944
Only Nicola can handle that
brutal stallion.

123
00:22:13,533 --> 00:22:17,403
Nicola is handy, we know that.

124
00:22:17,817 --> 00:22:22,196
If you send soldiers to Nicola to
support him...

125
00:22:22,196 --> 00:22:25,276
that will mess the whole Bithynia.

126
00:22:25,611 --> 00:22:31,531
You have to calculate the end.

127
00:22:35,535 --> 00:22:40,385
I won't send soldier to Nicola.

128
00:22:40,385 --> 00:22:44,535
I will send gold to Nicola
to take care of him.

129
00:22:59,922 --> 00:23:06,142
Thank my holy Lord that we
destroyed our enemies one by one.

130
00:23:07,958 --> 00:23:11,208
- Thanks to him.
- Thanks to him.

131
00:23:12,103 --> 00:23:16,623
Now, there's only Nicola left.

132
00:23:17,525 --> 00:23:21,895
Sooner or later, we'll take
care of him too.

133
00:23:22,000 --> 00:23:24,440
- Inshallah (If Allah permits.)
- Inshallah.

134
00:23:26,361 --> 00:23:27,961
Osman Bey...

135
00:23:28,001 --> 00:23:29,851
Yes, Umur Bey.

136
00:23:30,267 --> 00:23:34,227
Before I go back to my tent,
I have something to tell you.

137
00:23:36,782 --> 00:23:40,302
Time has proved you right, Osman Bey.

138
00:23:40,981 --> 00:23:45,171
While we remained
in the darkness of excuses...

139
00:23:45,464 --> 00:23:49,334
The light of the tradition shined on you.

140
00:23:50,292 --> 00:23:55,422
While we acted selfish,
arguing for nothing...

141
00:23:57,083 --> 00:24:01,373
You only cared our unitiy.

142
00:24:01,823 --> 00:24:07,493
We came and saw that you are the one.

143
00:24:08,142 --> 00:24:13,202
And you are the one to judge.

144
00:24:14,381 --> 00:24:16,231
Estagfurullah (not at all).

145
00:24:16,551 --> 00:24:18,771
Estagfurullah Umur Bey.

146
00:24:21,061 --> 00:24:26,091
The one who judges is...

147
00:24:26,813 --> 00:24:28,713
Allah.

148
00:24:31,544 --> 00:24:35,354
What we need to do is to work.

149
00:24:36,783 --> 00:24:40,013
Thank you, Osman Bey.
Thank you.

150
00:24:40,774 --> 00:24:43,044
We united the tribes.

151
00:24:43,179 --> 00:24:47,639
My Bey father and my Bey goes shoulder
to shoulder. No one can stop us.

152
00:24:50,008 --> 00:24:53,028
Our struggle has just getting started,
Malhun Hatun.

153
00:24:56,676 --> 00:25:00,236
Togay dies, another one comes.

154
00:25:01,272 --> 00:25:05,562
However, we won't stop!

155
00:25:06,386 --> 00:25:10,666
We will be riding high in the saddle
to the horizon we believe in.

156
00:25:18,003 --> 00:25:21,843
Togay messed up with the wrong people.

157
00:25:22,778 --> 00:25:26,078
He paid for it with his life.

158
00:25:29,603 --> 00:25:32,183
Osman killed Togay but...

159
00:25:32,562 --> 00:25:35,122
you send him to the death's door.

160
00:25:38,805 --> 00:25:42,125
Who do you think is the winner now?

161
00:25:42,579 --> 00:25:44,339
Is it Osman or you?

162
00:25:44,444 --> 00:25:47,524
Osman benefited as much as you did.

163
00:25:47,786 --> 00:25:52,736
Moreover, he gained dignity in front of
Turk Beys as he killed that barbar in Sogut.

164
00:25:53,704 --> 00:25:59,624
This Osman will blow up in
our hands, Nicola.

165
00:25:59,922 --> 00:26:04,802
Or he will bring us new opportunuties,
Yason.

166
00:26:11,225 --> 00:26:14,238
- Mikis.
- Sir.

167
00:26:14,238 --> 00:26:17,488
Mongol messenger came from
Konya to see you.

168
00:26:19,432 --> 00:26:22,162
Let our precious guest in.

169
00:26:31,327 --> 00:26:34,507
We are honoured, my messenger.
Welcome.

170
00:27:30,660 --> 00:27:33,160
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim.
(In the name of Allah, the merciful, the compassionate.)

171
00:27:58,694 --> 00:28:01,314
The warrior of Ghazis Bamsı Bey.

172
00:28:04,570 --> 00:28:07,160
The fellow of Ertugrul Bey.

173
00:28:08,603 --> 00:28:10,903
The head of Kayı Alps.

174
00:28:12,943 --> 00:28:16,553
You ended the enemy of our tribe.

175
00:28:19,526 --> 00:28:23,826
You did never let Kayıs down.

176
00:28:24,376 --> 00:28:25,686
Now...

177
00:28:28,645 --> 00:28:30,905
your sons...

178
00:28:34,248 --> 00:28:36,958
took revenge for you.

179
00:28:37,237 --> 00:28:40,017
We didn't let you down.

180
00:28:41,648 --> 00:28:46,938
You used to run to a war to another
without sleep.

181
00:28:47,613 --> 00:28:49,863
Now sleep well.

182
00:28:54,701 --> 00:28:57,191
Sleep well.

183
00:28:58,576 --> 00:29:00,636
Don't worry about us.

184
00:29:06,566 --> 00:29:09,426
Cerkutay, come.

185
00:29:10,366 --> 00:29:11,856
Come.

186
00:29:47,116 --> 00:29:50,166
You have just met Bamsı Bey.

187
00:29:52,104 --> 00:29:54,274
Yet you still cry.

188
00:29:55,863 --> 00:30:00,443
Think about what our feelings are.

189
00:30:06,700 --> 00:30:08,530
Okay.

190
00:30:10,273 --> 00:30:13,953
Don't be shy.
Pour out your heart.

191
00:30:24,758 --> 00:30:26,758
Don't worry about us.

192
00:30:29,428 --> 00:30:31,068
Father.

193
00:30:36,736 --> 00:30:39,216
I have your swords.

194
00:30:44,442 --> 00:30:47,642
I am trying to use them both.

195
00:30:48,956 --> 00:30:51,212
I clean your tent everyday.

196
00:30:51,212 --> 00:30:54,252
I wake up in the night and pray for you.

197
00:30:58,968 --> 00:31:04,108
If I have a son, I'll name him Bamsı.

198
00:31:05,226 --> 00:31:07,486
I'll tell him about you.

199
00:31:29,340 --> 00:31:31,230
You will.

200
00:31:32,389 --> 00:31:34,139
You will.

201
00:31:37,798 --> 00:31:39,538
You'll get married.

202
00:31:42,287 --> 00:31:44,557
You'll have children.

203
00:32:21,399 --> 00:32:23,349
Alps!

204
00:32:26,700 --> 00:32:29,180
We will be ready everytime.

205
00:32:30,945 --> 00:32:33,175
We shall not stop from now on!

206
00:32:33,243 --> 00:32:34,963
We shall not!

207
00:32:38,187 --> 00:32:43,337
We will continue until our swords break,
until the last drop of our blood.

208
00:32:45,709 --> 00:32:47,449
For Bamsı Bey!

209
00:32:51,309 --> 00:32:54,789
Allah-u Akbar!
(Allah is the greatest!)

210
00:32:56,515 --> 00:33:04,125
Allah-u Akbar!
(Allah is the greatest!)

211
00:33:18,828 --> 00:33:21,738
To be honest, messenger.

212
00:33:21,749 --> 00:33:23,522
I am shocked.

213
00:33:23,522 --> 00:33:26,102
How can such a loyal commander...

214
00:33:26,332 --> 00:33:29,422
rebel to Geyhatu?

215
00:33:30,326 --> 00:33:35,426
Ah Osman.
Togay called him Gokboru.

216
00:33:36,487 --> 00:33:42,287
It is a wolf that comes only in one
thousand years, something like that.

217
00:33:42,964 --> 00:33:45,964
I can now see what he meant.

218
00:33:46,178 --> 00:33:47,948
Gokboru hah?

219
00:33:49,447 --> 00:33:54,457
While Osman curshed Togay like a mouse
that raided his barn...

220
00:33:54,537 --> 00:33:57,567
He talked like a rebel, like a
threat to Geyhatu...

221
00:33:59,128 --> 00:34:04,588
not like a Bey who only pays
his taxes.

222
00:34:04,941 --> 00:34:08,941
So, he challanged Yargucu.

223
00:34:08,983 --> 00:34:14,623
Osman Bey will be trouble to you,
not to us.

224
00:34:16,450 --> 00:34:18,320
Governor Nicola.

225
00:34:19,539 --> 00:34:21,749
Sooner or later.

226
00:34:21,883 --> 00:34:24,053
He'll conquer your castle first.

227
00:34:25,029 --> 00:34:30,199
Like how his father conquered Karacahisar,
and like how he conquered Kulucahisar.

228
00:34:31,273 --> 00:34:33,803
The time passed.

229
00:34:33,977 --> 00:34:38,140
The tribes who rebels to Sultan and
Geyhatu...

230
00:34:38,140 --> 00:34:40,980
will come this land, won't they?

231
00:34:41,023 --> 00:34:42,643
Yes they will!

232
00:34:42,856 --> 00:34:46,816
Will Osman chase them?
He will.

233
00:34:47,018 --> 00:34:50,018
Will he pay tax to Geyhatu?
He won't!

234
00:34:50,132 --> 00:34:52,472
If my castle falls...

235
00:34:53,336 --> 00:34:56,806
Yargucu will be dead.

236
00:34:57,580 --> 00:34:59,770
Yes he will be.

237
00:35:00,462 --> 00:35:03,617
We can beat Osman with our
one finger.

238
00:35:03,617 --> 00:35:08,687
Oh, be careful there.

239
00:35:11,458 --> 00:35:15,978
Be careful, he may break that finger.

240
00:35:21,047 --> 00:35:23,987
We both want to stop Osman.

241
00:35:24,723 --> 00:35:27,203
It'll be good for both of us.

242
00:35:27,352 --> 00:35:31,092
A strong army will solve the problem.

243
00:35:31,727 --> 00:35:34,407
As you know, the best Turk...

244
00:35:35,863 --> 00:35:38,083
is the dead Turk.

245
00:35:38,213 --> 00:35:41,799
You know we don't want a war.

246
00:35:41,799 --> 00:35:43,789
Governor Nicola.

247
00:35:56,944 --> 00:35:59,074
What is your proposal...

248
00:35:59,673 --> 00:36:01,863
dear messenger?

249
00:36:04,449 --> 00:36:06,879
Governor Yargucu will support you...

250
00:36:06,882 --> 00:36:10,442
on the struggle between you and Osman.

251
00:36:11,426 --> 00:36:15,976
We have a saying.
- talks in Greek -

252
00:36:18,595 --> 00:36:21,565
Do not be anyone's toy.

253
00:36:22,551 --> 00:36:28,361
If you will, there must be a price.

254
00:36:30,893 --> 00:36:34,643
A carriage full of gold is on its way to
here from Konya.

255
00:36:38,125 --> 00:36:42,535
It will arrive in Inegol if I don't...

256
00:36:43,169 --> 00:36:45,509
stop it.

257
00:36:47,217 --> 00:36:49,297
Do you like it?

258
00:36:50,551 --> 00:36:53,221
Do you have a saying for this?

259
00:36:53,940 --> 00:36:56,870
Some lives must be lifeless.

260
00:36:58,743 --> 00:37:03,517
If glorious Yargucu is going to help me...

261
00:37:03,517 --> 00:37:06,502
to destroy Osman, I cannot refuse...

262
00:37:06,502 --> 00:37:08,562
dear messenger.

263
00:37:18,408 --> 00:37:23,438
Your loyalty will make Governor
Yargucu happy.

264
00:37:34,630 --> 00:37:38,680
Do not be anyone's toy.

265
00:37:58,001 --> 00:38:05,191
Welcome Osman Bey.
Welcome my Bey.

266
00:38:05,662 --> 00:38:07,562
Welcome my Osman Bey.

267
00:38:10,453 --> 00:38:13,863
Brother, I want to talk to my Beys.

268
00:38:13,884 --> 00:38:16,534
Eyvallah (okay) Osman Bey.
Baysungur.

269
00:38:17,563 --> 00:38:19,223
Turanalp!

270
00:38:22,107 --> 00:38:23,617
My Bey.

271
00:38:24,199 --> 00:38:26,059
You honored your name.

272
00:38:27,209 --> 00:38:31,459
We punished Togay,
we secured the justice.

273
00:38:31,939 --> 00:38:33,699
Eyvallah (thanks) my Bey.

274
00:38:34,204 --> 00:38:37,794
My only aim is to be a martyr in
the direction of your sword.

275
00:38:37,794 --> 00:38:40,804
Eyvallah. (thanks).
Eyvallah.

276
00:38:43,619 --> 00:38:49,499
You said he couldn't manage but, he
brought us Togay. Mashallah (praise be).

277
00:38:51,815 --> 00:38:55,035
And Osman Bey sees it.

278
00:39:00,245 --> 00:39:05,375
Now, As Osman Bey's Alp...
You need to do what you have to do.

279
00:39:07,381 --> 00:39:10,261
Eyvallah brother.
You are right.

280
00:39:10,841 --> 00:39:12,841
Oh my brother.

281
00:39:13,566 --> 00:39:16,516
This is how Osman Bey's alp acts.

282
00:39:40,077 --> 00:39:42,887
Put the rugs in a different chest, Alaca.

283
00:39:45,262 --> 00:39:47,822
- What are these for?
- Keep up.

284
00:39:49,299 --> 00:39:52,729
These are all my mother's handcraft.

285
00:39:54,097 --> 00:39:57,957
As we told her to stop, she
would stare at us...

286
00:39:58,421 --> 00:40:02,371
and say "These will decorate a
bride's dowery."

287
00:40:04,131 --> 00:40:07,921
Being Umur Bey's Hatun requires diligince.

288
00:40:08,703 --> 00:40:14,343
She used to control the whole tribe.
She used to overcome.

289
00:40:14,993 --> 00:40:18,203
She used to stitch these if she has any
time left.

290
00:40:20,590 --> 00:40:23,100
You passed away early, my valiant mother.

291
00:40:28,656 --> 00:40:32,666
Store the ornamental rugs in a differnet
chest, Alaca.

292
00:40:33,171 --> 00:40:36,611
Why are we doing this, Malhun Hatun?
I really wonder.

293
00:40:37,168 --> 00:40:42,788
They have been in the chest since we
came here. I want to please my mother.

294
00:40:43,353 --> 00:40:45,783
They shall decorate Osman Bey's tent.

295
00:40:46,045 --> 00:40:48,505
May my mother rest in peace.

296
00:40:51,823 --> 00:40:55,443
Does Bala Hatun know about this?

297
00:40:57,217 --> 00:41:00,567
She doesn't need to know.
The tent is Osman Bey's.

298
00:41:00,735 --> 00:41:02,965
I am a Hatun of this tent.

299
00:41:53,423 --> 00:41:56,893
Did you settle down in there?

300
00:42:14,709 --> 00:42:17,119
Of course I did.

301
00:42:24,175 --> 00:42:29,445
Not only Osman, but also his whole
tribe is in my hands.

302
00:42:29,767 --> 00:42:33,887
I'll cause Turks' extinction
sooner or later.

303
00:42:34,119 --> 00:42:38,619
But first, I'll destroy Osman's hopes
to have a child.

304
00:42:39,034 --> 00:42:40,504
With...

305
00:42:42,886 --> 00:42:45,966
with your soft hands.

306
00:42:52,209 --> 00:42:55,339
Malhun loves me like a sister.

307
00:42:55,907 --> 00:42:58,707
She trusts me, she listens to me.

308
00:43:01,401 --> 00:43:06,021
My soft eyes are enough to scratch their
eyes out.

309
00:43:06,524 --> 00:43:10,264
Zoe, my little venomous snake.

310
00:43:10,899 --> 00:43:12,779
Tell me.

311
00:43:17,046 --> 00:43:21,536
Where should I begin?
Malhun Hatun, Alaca...

312
00:43:21,846 --> 00:43:23,696
Umur Bey...

313
00:43:26,143 --> 00:43:28,003
Goktug.

314
00:43:32,621 --> 00:43:34,621
Silly lover.

315
00:43:34,870 --> 00:43:38,468
Is this silly lover under your spell?

316
00:43:38,468 --> 00:43:42,518
Spell? Let's call it witchery.

317
00:43:42,775 --> 00:43:48,335
Zoe, I want you to enhance your contacts.

318
00:43:48,399 --> 00:43:53,149
Be my shadow until I hit the
last time.

319
00:43:54,045 --> 00:43:59,075
Not only what you hear and see...
I want to know what you smell, what you feel.

320
00:44:02,170 --> 00:44:03,720
What I smell

321
00:44:06,871 --> 00:44:08,481
is sheep.

322
00:44:09,318 --> 00:44:14,078
What I feel is the taste of
the pain I'll give them.

323
00:44:18,619 --> 00:44:21,769
Trust your loyal servant Zoe, sir.

324
00:44:23,936 --> 00:44:27,876
I won't get out of there
without my prey.

325
00:44:29,205 --> 00:44:31,585
Goktug must have missed you.

326
00:44:31,878 --> 00:44:33,678
Go.

327
00:45:00,898 --> 00:45:04,008
No, this silence is not good.

328
00:45:04,875 --> 00:45:08,585
Governor Yargucu must have learned
we took Togay.

329
00:45:10,917 --> 00:45:15,887
My Bey, are those cruels going to
attack us with an army?

330
00:45:16,617 --> 00:45:19,477
Mongols have many troubles
to deal with.

331
00:45:19,909 --> 00:45:24,369
Our Turkmen brothers support us.

332
00:45:24,834 --> 00:45:29,704
In this mess, they can't
gather an army to attack us.

333
00:45:31,122 --> 00:45:35,372
However, we are going to take
precautions.

334
00:45:38,394 --> 00:45:40,044
Can I come in my Bey?

335
00:45:40,258 --> 00:45:41,778
Come!

336
00:45:46,939 --> 00:45:50,689
My Bey, Mongols sent a messenger.

337
00:45:52,013 --> 00:45:54,683
Speak of the devil, and he appears.

338
00:46:05,979 --> 00:46:07,919
Let him come.

339
00:46:26,793 --> 00:46:31,423
I came here under the order of glorious
Ilhanlı State's holy heir Yargucu.

340
00:46:32,875 --> 00:46:34,525
Speak.

341
00:46:35,535 --> 00:46:37,845
You know why I am here.

342
00:46:38,768 --> 00:46:41,828
You executed Togay, Osman Bey.

343
00:46:42,222 --> 00:46:47,082
That's fine.
What else does your governor want?

344
00:46:47,991 --> 00:46:49,861
The price.

345
00:46:53,886 --> 00:46:56,086
The price, huh?

346
00:46:57,293 --> 00:46:59,223
The price.

347
00:47:03,584 --> 00:47:06,014
What is the price? Tell me.

348
00:47:07,567 --> 00:47:11,667
You'll pay your three-year tax
in three days.

349
00:47:18,185 --> 00:47:22,765
This is the punihment you are given.

350
00:47:45,897 --> 00:47:47,717
Three days huh?

351
00:47:48,425 --> 00:47:50,095
Three days.

352
00:47:51,530 --> 00:47:54,260
If you don't deliver the gold in time...

353
00:47:54,704 --> 00:47:57,514
It'll mean you violated the
agreement with Yargucu.

354
00:47:58,889 --> 00:48:01,379
Ilhanlı State will not come to
take gold...

355
00:48:03,805 --> 00:48:06,085
We'll come to kill.

356
00:48:23,181 --> 00:48:25,411
Three days it is.

357
00:48:26,344 --> 00:48:28,574
You shall leave.

358
00:48:33,018 --> 00:48:38,388
We are going to prepare the gold.

359
00:48:54,497 --> 00:48:56,557
So, my Beys.

360
00:48:58,478 --> 00:49:00,168
Tell me.

361
00:49:00,436 --> 00:49:02,626
You all heard.

362
00:49:03,484 --> 00:49:05,404
What do you think?

363
00:49:05,684 --> 00:49:08,774
Let's say we paid them...

364
00:49:08,974 --> 00:49:12,684
What are we going to do?
We can't afford any of the needs.

365
00:49:13,323 --> 00:49:16,193
We'll have to stop the charities
in Sogut.

366
00:49:16,370 --> 00:49:18,570
We can't even afford Alps.

367
00:49:18,959 --> 00:49:22,299
And they won't stop, they'll
want more.

368
00:49:22,671 --> 00:49:25,471
Our only choice is war.

369
00:49:25,848 --> 00:49:28,088
They are cornering us.

370
00:49:28,251 --> 00:49:29,921
This is why they want too much.

371
00:49:30,872 --> 00:49:32,573
They want us to fail to pay.

372
00:49:32,573 --> 00:49:37,243
They are trying hold us responsible
for the war.

373
00:49:40,669 --> 00:49:43,339
I have an agreement with Sultan.

374
00:49:46,024 --> 00:49:51,074
It is not appropriate for me to do
something without his information.

375
00:49:52,974 --> 00:49:54,744
After all...

376
00:49:56,111 --> 00:49:59,661
After all, he risked his throne to
support us.

377
00:50:02,268 --> 00:50:06,418
I'll think it through.

378
00:50:07,814 --> 00:50:10,544
Then I'll decide.

379
00:50:24,858 --> 00:50:28,328
Governer Yargucu's gold
will arrive tomorrow.

380
00:50:28,354 --> 00:50:32,538
Dimitri, you'll welcome the soldiers.

381
00:50:32,538 --> 00:50:35,988
I can't rest until I see the gold
in my castle.

382
00:50:36,063 --> 00:50:37,923
How can I do it?

383
00:50:39,710 --> 00:50:42,140
I like to take precautions.

384
00:50:42,572 --> 00:50:46,422
Take precautions so that
you can sleep well, Dimitri.

385
00:50:46,963 --> 00:50:49,033
Yes, sir.

386
00:50:51,160 --> 00:50:53,797
We'll create a new army with the gold, sir.

387
00:50:53,797 --> 00:50:58,027
I'll create an army of randy fighters,
not an army of lazy peasants, Helen.

388
00:50:58,183 --> 00:51:02,013
You'll go to the bazaar of fighters
with the gold.

389
00:51:02,207 --> 00:51:06,283
We'll create an army of Maceds. Catalans,
the pirates, the barbarians who..

390
00:51:06,283 --> 00:51:09,703
are ready to do anything for us.

391
00:51:11,444 --> 00:51:15,837
Dimitri, take your soldiers and leave.

392
00:51:15,837 --> 00:51:18,737
Bring me my gold safe and sound.

393
00:51:19,353 --> 00:51:21,303
Yes sir.

394
00:51:23,645 --> 00:51:27,295
In this land where the tables can turn
upside down anytime...

395
00:51:27,295 --> 00:51:31,295
Togay's death brought us gold, Helen.

396
00:51:31,389 --> 00:51:34,379
Now it's time to use that opportunity,
Nicola.

397
00:51:34,465 --> 00:51:38,575
We don't have a second to lose.
Start working already.

398
00:51:38,878 --> 00:51:42,788
Helena, we are stronger than before.

399
00:51:43,092 --> 00:51:45,912
We have eyes in the tribe.

400
00:51:46,839 --> 00:51:49,399
Zoe has sharp eyes.

401
00:51:49,727 --> 00:51:52,177
But her teeth are sharper.

402
00:52:34,614 --> 00:52:39,054
The immigrants will be fed in the cook
tent until they can earn their keep.

403
00:52:39,911 --> 00:52:42,191
We have more expenses, my Osman.

404
00:52:48,796 --> 00:52:51,556
As long as Sogut grows...

405
00:52:52,693 --> 00:52:55,143
our expenses can be more, that's fine,
my Bala.

406
00:52:55,545 --> 00:52:57,813
We'll take care of it,
Inshallah (if Allah permits).

407
00:52:57,813 --> 00:52:59,323
We will.

408
00:53:01,278 --> 00:53:02,788
We will.

409
00:53:07,806 --> 00:53:09,456
My Bala...

410
00:53:10,514 --> 00:53:13,294
I want Malhun Hatun to come to Sogut, too.

411
00:53:13,455 --> 00:53:15,965
I want her to help on cook tent.

412
00:53:16,834 --> 00:53:19,464
Gonca helps me, thank her.

413
00:53:19,968 --> 00:53:22,968
- I don't need anyone else.
- Malhun Hatun can join you.

414
00:53:23,113 --> 00:53:26,123
She can help you,
she'll be handy.

415
00:53:28,391 --> 00:53:32,891
If you say so.

416
00:53:36,263 --> 00:53:38,123
My Bala...

417
00:53:38,415 --> 00:53:41,435
It's not easy.

418
00:53:42,592 --> 00:53:45,342
She used to do the all work in
her tent.

419
00:53:45,401 --> 00:53:50,401
She was to decide, she was to fight
without a Bey.

420
00:53:50,639 --> 00:53:53,749
Now, she is just sitting in the tent.

421
00:53:56,066 --> 00:53:58,073
She is not used to this.

422
00:53:58,073 --> 00:53:59,893
We have to give her some
space to work.

423
00:54:01,564 --> 00:54:05,944
This is true.
She is this tent's Hatun as well.

424
00:54:07,131 --> 00:54:09,201
She has every right.

425
00:54:12,928 --> 00:54:15,008
Can I come in my Bey?

426
00:54:16,897 --> 00:54:20,607
Be patient my Bala.
Be patient.

427
00:54:30,092 --> 00:54:32,022
Come Baysungur.

428
00:54:33,574 --> 00:54:36,944
Be patient Bala.
Be patient.

429
00:54:41,007 --> 00:54:43,267
A letter from our Sultan, my Bey.

430
00:55:45,891 --> 00:55:48,201
Is everything ready, my Gonca?

431
00:55:48,472 --> 00:55:51,152
Don't worry, my Bala.
Everything is ready.

432
00:55:51,176 --> 00:55:53,096
Okay, the tribe is entrusted to you.

433
00:56:01,124 --> 00:56:05,124
Malhun Hatun, I am going to the
cook tent. You shall come with me.

434
00:56:06,561 --> 00:56:09,081
Of course, that'd be great.

435
00:56:09,844 --> 00:56:13,194
I have other things to do, Bala Hatun.

436
00:56:14,237 --> 00:56:18,100
I'll come when I am available.

437
00:56:18,100 --> 00:56:21,030
We can solve if there's any problem.

438
00:56:21,517 --> 00:56:24,267
Cook tent has no problem to solve.

439
00:56:24,371 --> 00:56:29,401
If you want to help like everyone else do,
you are welcomed.

440
00:56:32,657 --> 00:56:36,763
Right. People should compete
when it comes to charity.

441
00:56:36,763 --> 00:56:41,683
Let's leave, Bala Hatun. Malhun Hatun will
join when she is ready.

442
00:56:42,689 --> 00:56:44,509
See you.

443
00:56:44,900 --> 00:56:46,470
Let's go.

444
00:57:00,894 --> 00:57:02,794
See you.

445
00:57:32,616 --> 00:57:34,846
We finished fast.
Mashallah (praise be).

446
00:57:35,007 --> 00:57:37,269
I have never seen a bigger dowery
in my life.

447
00:57:37,269 --> 00:57:39,219
Your turn is next.

448
00:57:41,191 --> 00:57:46,541
So, Zoe, shall we have an Alp from Kayı
tribe for you and Alaca.

449
00:57:51,851 --> 00:57:53,841
Alaca Hatun?

450
00:57:54,598 --> 00:57:57,728
There are enough alps in
Umur Bey's tent, Malhun Hatun.

451
00:57:58,497 --> 00:58:01,427
Calm down, Alaca. Okay.

452
00:58:04,070 --> 00:58:07,280
There are chests to open.
We have to settle down.

453
00:58:07,478 --> 00:58:10,298
Finish before it gets dark.

454
00:59:37,823 --> 00:59:39,558
- Boran.
- My Bey.

455
00:59:39,558 --> 00:59:42,232
Wait until Mongols move away.

456
00:59:42,232 --> 00:59:44,362
Yes my Bey.

457
00:59:58,589 --> 01:00:01,069
Cover the chests with these red cloths.

458
01:00:16,397 --> 01:00:17,977
What are these?

459
01:00:18,054 --> 01:00:19,824
What are you doing?

460
01:00:20,476 --> 01:00:24,390
We are changing the rugs.

461
01:00:24,390 --> 01:00:27,360
Did anyone let you do that?

462
01:00:32,749 --> 01:00:35,366
We asked Malhun Hatun, Gonca Hatun.

463
01:00:35,366 --> 01:00:38,046
Do you hear what you say, Hatun?

464
01:00:38,323 --> 01:00:41,503
Don't you know who is the Hatun
of this tent?

465
01:00:46,354 --> 01:00:49,004
Am I not this tent's Hatun?

466
01:00:54,120 --> 01:00:55,980
Don't you know that?

467
01:01:03,221 --> 01:01:04,721
You are.

468
01:01:05,050 --> 01:01:07,272
Of course you are.

469
01:01:07,272 --> 01:01:09,752
They are performing my order.

470
01:01:10,715 --> 01:01:13,725
If you came to help, come help.

471
01:01:13,966 --> 01:01:16,426
If you won't, leave.

472
01:01:22,773 --> 01:01:25,433
Go on, Hatuns.

473
01:01:29,419 --> 01:01:31,789
Do you want to say anything, Hatun?

474
01:01:35,454 --> 01:01:37,114
Here is the door.

475
01:02:30,920 --> 01:02:33,770
Get ready! Get in the position!

476
01:02:55,294 --> 01:02:57,354
Get in the position!

477
01:06:01,722 --> 01:06:03,922
Come here, Dimitri.

478
01:07:35,622 --> 01:07:37,362
Kill me.

479
01:07:38,502 --> 01:07:40,592
Nikola will take care of you.

480
01:07:41,108 --> 01:07:42,958
Tell Nikola that...

481
01:07:43,492 --> 01:07:47,032
even if he hides behind the Mongols...

482
01:07:47,244 --> 01:07:53,174
I will be the one who kills him.

483
01:08:44,272 --> 01:08:45,362
My Bey is coming.

484
01:08:59,739 --> 01:09:02,779
We saved our golds from the heathens.

485
01:09:03,122 --> 01:09:06,342
Now, it's time to use them for good.

486
01:09:06,719 --> 01:09:09,459
Come on, Alps!
We're going back to the tent.

487
01:09:13,711 --> 01:09:15,131
Come on, Alps!

488
01:09:19,124 --> 01:09:21,114
Come on, Alps!

489
01:09:37,717 --> 01:09:38,827
Thank you.

490
01:09:44,872 --> 01:09:46,022
Bala.

491
01:09:50,547 --> 01:09:51,457
My Gonca.

492
01:09:51,935 --> 01:09:54,055
- Why are you in such a hurry?
- My Bala.

493
01:09:54,297 --> 01:09:57,127
- You should come to the tent.
- What happened?

494
01:10:00,590 --> 01:10:02,160
Malhun Hatun.

495
01:10:07,285 --> 01:10:13,645
How did he know? How did Osman
know that the golds were there?

496
01:10:13,972 --> 01:10:17,972
How? How did he learn?

497
01:10:18,045 --> 01:10:21,956
How did he learn? How did he learn?

498
01:10:22,026 --> 01:10:25,236
- How did he learn?
- Dimitri doesn't know that, sir.

499
01:10:25,292 --> 01:10:30,532
Helen, shut up!
Shut up!

500
01:10:42,893 --> 01:10:45,593
Sir, we have a letter from our Emperor.

501
01:10:59,049 --> 01:11:00,439
Nikola.

502
01:11:03,138 --> 01:11:04,648
Nikola.

503
01:11:09,908 --> 01:11:11,918
Nikola.

504
01:11:18,468 --> 01:11:20,388
The Emperor...

505
01:11:22,737 --> 01:11:26,737
wants me to go to İznik to talk to my son.

506
01:11:28,166 --> 01:11:29,166
Why?

507
01:11:29,287 --> 01:11:32,507
Every human seals his
or her own fate, Helen.

508
01:11:33,951 --> 01:11:37,351
I'm going to read my own fate.

509
01:12:01,689 --> 01:12:03,599
We did good, Osman Bey.

510
01:12:06,439 --> 01:12:10,439
Sultan Mesut wrote that the governor
will send Nikola the golds.

511
01:12:13,167 --> 01:12:16,437
He wants to punish you.

512
01:12:17,974 --> 01:12:19,834
What will we do, Osman Bey?

513
01:12:19,933 --> 01:12:23,093
We will have the
golds that the governor sent.

514
01:12:23,288 --> 01:12:24,838
Osman Bey...

515
01:12:25,060 --> 01:12:28,850
won't it make the
Ilkhanate angry towards us?

516
01:12:28,926 --> 01:12:32,056
We won't have the Mongols' golds, brother.

517
01:12:33,057 --> 01:12:35,947
We will have Nikola's golds.

518
01:12:36,817 --> 01:12:38,577
We killed two birds with one stone.

519
01:12:38,712 --> 01:12:41,422
We prevented Nikola
from going stronger and...

520
01:12:41,570 --> 01:12:45,500
we will pay our taxes to Mongols.

521
01:12:46,491 --> 01:12:48,881
With their own golds.

522
01:13:15,608 --> 01:13:17,538
Malhun Hatun.

523
01:13:22,291 --> 01:13:25,201
How could you do that without telling me?

524
01:13:25,821 --> 01:13:29,261
Keep calm, Bala Hatun.

525
01:13:30,899 --> 01:13:33,459
You shouldn't be that angry.

526
01:13:33,522 --> 01:13:36,192
I brought some stuff from my dowery.

527
01:13:49,756 --> 01:13:52,706
Malhun Hatun.
It's a Bey tent.

528
01:13:52,921 --> 01:13:55,521
Everything has a meaning here.

529
01:13:55,563 --> 01:13:58,173
You can't bring everything you want.

530
01:14:18,328 --> 01:14:22,728
As you said, Bala Hatun.
Everything is more meaningful now.

531
01:14:24,922 --> 01:14:28,322
It's seen that Malhun Hatun is here.

532
01:14:29,460 --> 01:14:32,000
Is that why you're here?

533
01:14:34,707 --> 01:14:37,907
Are you here to spoil everything?

534
01:14:39,003 --> 01:14:42,483
You have your own tent, Hatun.
You do whatever you wish there.

535
01:14:42,502 --> 01:14:44,792
You shall not mess here.

536
01:14:47,814 --> 01:14:49,684
Bala Hatun.

537
01:15:09,669 --> 01:15:11,249
Beys are back.

538
01:15:11,568 --> 01:15:13,888
Let's meet them.

539
01:15:48,142 --> 01:15:50,042
Thank you!

540
01:15:59,687 --> 01:16:01,407
Thank you!

541
01:16:06,553 --> 01:16:11,453
- May your war be holy, my Bey.
- Thank you.

542
01:16:14,021 --> 01:16:16,731
Mashallah!

543
01:16:48,461 --> 01:16:51,001
May your war be holy, Osman Bey.

544
01:16:51,305 --> 01:16:54,655
Thank you, Malhun Hatun.

545
01:16:54,853 --> 01:16:57,413
We have got some news.

546
01:16:57,536 --> 01:16:59,626
You hurt the heathens again.

547
01:16:59,726 --> 01:17:03,156
We'll shed more blood until we take...

548
01:17:03,786 --> 01:17:05,736
Bamsı Bey's revenge.

549
01:17:06,130 --> 01:17:10,130
- May Allah protect your sword.
- Amin. Inshallah.

550
01:17:22,723 --> 01:17:26,083
I made food for you.

551
01:17:26,706 --> 01:17:30,086
Come to my meal if you're hungry.

552
01:17:43,275 --> 01:17:46,895
I should talk to my Beys.

553
01:17:47,364 --> 01:17:49,474
Later, Inshallah.

554
01:17:55,118 --> 01:17:56,958
- My Bey.
- My Bala.

555
01:18:00,348 --> 01:18:02,258
May your war be holy.

556
01:18:03,047 --> 01:18:05,547
Thank you.

557
01:18:45,465 --> 01:18:49,465
- Salam Alaikum, Master Davut.
- Alaikum Salam.

558
01:18:51,135 --> 01:18:54,025
- May it be easy.
- Do it if it is easy.

559
01:18:58,238 --> 01:18:59,878
It's my father's job.

560
01:19:00,920 --> 01:19:03,000
Hit then.

561
01:19:10,250 --> 01:19:13,370
- Mashallah.
- Thank you.

562
01:19:15,505 --> 01:19:20,355
- Tell me, what did happen?
- We got the golds for Nikola.

563
01:19:20,490 --> 01:19:22,600
Good.

564
01:19:22,800 --> 01:19:25,400
- Allah is right.
- Allah is eternal.

565
01:19:25,670 --> 01:19:35,030
- Allah is right.
- Allah is eternal.

566
01:19:35,754 --> 01:19:39,784
- Salam Alaikum, Master Davut.
- Alaikum Salam.

567
01:19:40,343 --> 01:19:43,603
- Osman Bey is waiting for you.
- Why?

568
01:20:02,468 --> 01:20:05,788
You did good, Turan Alp.

569
01:20:07,587 --> 01:20:10,117
It's not a big deal.

570
01:20:10,606 --> 01:20:14,976
Don't say that. You're
good for a new comer.

571
01:20:15,497 --> 01:20:19,597
I am the soldier of Kayı Tent.

572
01:20:20,907 --> 01:20:24,687
Kayı Tent's duties are hard.

573
01:20:26,410 --> 01:20:29,150
The fate is the same.

574
01:20:29,310 --> 01:20:33,490
We are martyrs if we die, we
are Ghazis if we stay.

575
01:20:34,098 --> 01:20:41,388
- Allah is right.
- Allah is eternal.

576
01:20:44,364 --> 01:20:47,144
Mongols wanted to...

577
01:20:47,950 --> 01:20:50,200
empower Nikola.

578
01:20:50,518 --> 01:20:54,558
He wanted to get soldiers with
these golds and attack us.

579
01:20:54,967 --> 01:20:57,817
You spoiled their plans, my Bey.

580
01:20:58,002 --> 01:20:59,902
They shouldn't be angrier.

581
01:21:00,167 --> 01:21:04,697
We didn't get these golds from the
Mongols. Why do they be angry?

582
01:21:05,679 --> 01:21:09,169
We got them from our enemies.

583
01:21:10,023 --> 01:21:11,623
And...

584
01:21:12,778 --> 01:21:16,448
the golds that Mongols want from us...

585
01:21:17,471 --> 01:21:21,101
here are the golds.

586
01:21:21,605 --> 01:21:25,685
They won't like it as they
will have their own golds.

587
01:21:27,236 --> 01:21:34,076
They will see what happens if
they play trick to Kayıs.

588
01:21:34,430 --> 01:21:35,610
Yes.

589
01:21:36,211 --> 01:21:39,301
What you have done will be known
by everyone.

590
01:21:39,567 --> 01:21:42,337
Our Ghazis will be proud of you.

591
01:21:43,778 --> 01:21:46,938
More Ghazis will join us.

592
01:21:48,728 --> 01:21:51,188
We will be ready.

593
01:21:51,598 --> 01:21:54,878
We will have thousands of...

594
01:21:55,700 --> 01:21:58,540
soldiers and Ghazis.

595
01:22:01,918 --> 01:22:04,548
That's what my father wanted.

596
01:22:04,818 --> 01:22:05,668
Inshallah.

597
01:22:05,716 --> 01:22:08,746
We will be united.

598
01:22:08,883 --> 01:22:11,583
Thank you, brother.

599
01:22:12,404 --> 01:22:16,884
We will move step by step
and we will be careful.

600
01:22:20,267 --> 01:22:25,467
If Nikola is that closer to Mongols...

601
01:22:26,151 --> 01:22:28,321
it will continue.

602
01:22:29,039 --> 01:22:31,989
However, we will be careful.

603
01:22:33,244 --> 01:22:35,814
We will destroy Nikola...

604
01:22:36,402 --> 01:22:38,982
without letting Mongols know.

605
01:22:39,890 --> 01:22:42,250
May Allah make you powerful, Osman Bey.

606
01:22:42,577 --> 01:22:44,807
If you'll excuse me.

607
01:22:45,558 --> 01:22:48,608
I do.

608
01:22:59,638 --> 01:23:04,308
Send these golds to our Sultan, to Konya.

609
01:23:05,352 --> 01:23:08,022
Your command, my Bey.

610
01:23:14,782 --> 01:23:17,532
We will go to Sheikh Edebalı's lodge
tonight...

611
01:23:18,537 --> 01:23:21,347
together.

612
01:23:23,848 --> 01:23:26,488
Your command, my Bey.

613
01:23:48,696 --> 01:23:50,496
Akça Dervish.

614
01:23:51,154 --> 01:23:54,264
We have talked about justice.

615
01:23:55,343 --> 01:23:59,453
What is justice?

616
01:24:00,521 --> 01:24:05,561
Something stays where it
belongs, that is justice.

617
01:24:09,837 --> 01:24:15,427
What is injustice?

618
01:24:16,363 --> 01:24:21,393
It's putting something
where it doesn't belong to.

619
01:24:22,190 --> 01:24:24,300
Yes.

620
01:24:26,439 --> 01:24:28,569
Now...

621
01:24:29,095 --> 01:24:31,905
tell me, Kumral Abdal.

622
01:24:33,184 --> 01:24:37,284
When will injustice be legitimate?

623
01:24:39,159 --> 01:24:41,779
Never, my Sheikh.

624
01:24:42,427 --> 01:24:46,427
What if it is for Allah's consent?

625
01:24:50,989 --> 01:24:54,389
Injustice can't happen...

626
01:24:55,275 --> 01:24:58,205
even if it's for Allah.

627
01:24:59,179 --> 01:25:01,219
Yes.

628
01:25:08,683 --> 01:25:10,283
You tell me, Osman Bey.

629
01:25:11,717 --> 01:25:16,687
Can you do injustice for the state's good?

630
01:25:17,454 --> 01:25:19,184
The state...

631
01:25:19,684 --> 01:25:22,294
provides justice, my Sheikh.

632
01:25:25,863 --> 01:25:31,073
Injustice can't be a thing
what state does.

633
01:25:36,303 --> 01:25:40,303
Will an Alp do injustice...

634
01:25:41,557 --> 01:25:45,557
for a Bey's good?

635
01:25:49,602 --> 01:25:53,152
No, my Sheikh.
He shouldn't.

636
01:25:56,100 --> 01:26:01,120
Even if it is towards a heathen?

637
01:26:07,000 --> 01:26:08,960
He shouldn't, my Sheikh.

638
01:26:13,277 --> 01:26:16,067
Mashallah.
Mashallah.

639
01:26:21,165 --> 01:26:22,815
My Sheikh...

640
01:26:23,882 --> 01:26:28,922
We will come again
tomorrow with Boran Alp.

641
01:26:30,290 --> 01:26:35,190
And we will establish
justice in front of the lodge.

642
01:27:27,752 --> 01:27:30,222
Are you stealing food again, Cerkutay?

643
01:27:39,168 --> 01:27:41,298
I always eat at this time

644
01:27:44,164 --> 01:27:47,074
Bamsı Bey would eat at this time.

645
01:28:01,871 --> 01:28:04,101
Isn't a plate enough for you?

646
01:28:06,422 --> 01:28:07,962
Not for me.

647
01:28:09,059 --> 01:28:10,699
For Bamsı Bey.

648
01:28:17,561 --> 01:28:18,631
Bamsı Bey...

649
01:28:20,037 --> 01:28:22,377
For Bamsı Bey?

650
01:28:23,457 --> 01:28:24,877
I know, Aygül.

651
01:28:26,720 --> 01:28:29,640
Bamsı Bey is martryed.

652
01:28:32,833 --> 01:28:35,643
However, I can't accept it.

653
01:28:41,577 --> 01:28:43,077
Cerkutay...

654
01:28:51,113 --> 01:28:52,903
Some wounds...

655
01:28:58,691 --> 01:29:02,691
never heal, I know.

656
01:29:08,865 --> 01:29:10,785
In Bamsı Bey's tent...

657
01:29:13,318 --> 01:29:15,698
it's hard to live without him, right?

658
01:29:19,804 --> 01:29:23,154
I'm alone too.

659
01:29:24,509 --> 01:29:27,549
In a tent, alone.

660
01:29:28,907 --> 01:29:31,247
I think of so many things.

661
01:29:34,497 --> 01:29:37,557
Do you think I don't know that, mad girl?

662
01:29:39,710 --> 01:29:42,320
You're right.

663
01:29:45,907 --> 01:29:50,567
I know what you do in the tent.

664
01:29:52,061 --> 01:29:53,971
Don't think too much.

665
01:29:55,437 --> 01:29:59,437
Eat your food.

666
01:30:02,794 --> 01:30:04,224
Stop.

667
01:30:38,075 --> 01:30:39,035
Isn't it for...

668
01:30:40,697 --> 01:30:42,657
Bamsı Bey?

669
01:30:44,988 --> 01:30:49,438
He won't be angry as I give it to you.

670
01:31:34,550 --> 01:31:35,650
My Bala.

671
01:31:36,581 --> 01:31:39,631
How are the things going in cook tent?
Is everything okay?

672
01:31:40,524 --> 01:31:44,524
Everyone's needs are fulfilled.

673
01:31:46,531 --> 01:31:48,921
Did Malhun Hatun help?

674
01:31:52,553 --> 01:31:54,873
She couldn't come.

675
01:32:07,256 --> 01:32:09,636
She had more important job in her tent.

676
01:32:10,159 --> 01:32:11,649
What is that?

677
01:32:11,855 --> 01:32:15,405
She wanted some of our stuff
in our tent to change.

678
01:32:18,897 --> 01:32:20,657
She didn't like them, I guess.

679
01:32:35,511 --> 01:32:38,201
Everyone has a different taste.

680
01:32:39,749 --> 01:32:43,749
She wanted to make some changes.

681
01:32:47,296 --> 01:32:51,296
She is the Hatun of this tent too.

682
01:32:53,714 --> 01:32:56,374
She wanted to show herself.

683
01:33:11,323 --> 01:33:13,313
Now...

684
01:33:19,569 --> 01:33:23,149
have you heard of the sword of goodness?

685
01:33:25,809 --> 01:33:27,869
Tell me.

686
01:33:34,174 --> 01:33:38,454
Once upon a time, there was
a generous Sultan.

687
01:33:38,722 --> 01:33:43,852
This Sultan heard that there was someone
more generous than him.

688
01:33:44,477 --> 01:33:46,727
He was so angry!

689
01:33:47,772 --> 01:33:50,452
Who is this man who is
more generous than me, he said.

690
01:33:54,123 --> 01:33:57,423
Sultan was...

691
01:33:57,494 --> 01:34:02,614
becoming more jealous and jealous.

692
01:34:03,918 --> 01:34:05,748
Then...

693
01:34:05,871 --> 01:34:10,001
he said his executioner that
he should kill that man!

694
01:34:10,095 --> 01:34:14,425
I have to be the most generous
man in this world, he said.

695
01:34:20,437 --> 01:34:22,557
Have some.

696
01:34:29,266 --> 01:34:31,196
You too.

697
01:34:34,642 --> 01:34:36,572
Enjoy it.

698
01:34:42,390 --> 01:34:47,110
- Shouldn't you thank her?
- Thank you.

699
01:34:59,569 --> 01:35:03,719
Sultan sent...

700
01:35:04,196 --> 01:35:08,196
the executioner to the man.
However...

701
01:35:08,999 --> 01:35:12,589
the executioner was
the guest of the man who he would kill.

702
01:35:12,643 --> 01:35:16,113
He was treated so well by this man.

703
01:35:16,597 --> 01:35:20,597
Then he learnt that he
was the man who he would kill!

704
01:35:24,588 --> 01:35:26,348
May it be easy.

705
01:35:27,377 --> 01:35:28,847
Zoe.

706
01:35:32,586 --> 01:35:34,106
Thank you.

707
01:35:38,719 --> 01:35:42,609
I wonder what happens at the end of the
story that Kumral Abdal tells.

708
01:35:44,386 --> 01:35:48,386
I know what happens.
Kumral Abdal has told me once.

709
01:35:49,315 --> 01:35:51,735
You should tell me one day.

710
01:35:54,325 --> 01:35:57,285
Of course, I will.

711
01:36:03,370 --> 01:36:05,220
I see you love children.

712
01:36:05,496 --> 01:36:07,856
Of course I do.

713
01:36:08,053 --> 01:36:11,533
Their cheeks are sweeter than sherbet.

714
01:36:11,917 --> 01:36:15,287
They are the guests coming from
the heaven.

715
01:36:18,861 --> 01:36:21,151
The guest from the heaven.

716
01:36:23,813 --> 01:36:25,873
The guest from the heaven.

717
01:36:50,133 --> 01:36:52,193
I should go now.

718
01:36:59,830 --> 01:37:01,880
You couldn't say it again!

719
01:37:02,821 --> 01:37:05,761
When will you tell her, Göktuğ?

720
01:37:09,573 --> 01:37:13,763
When the executioner
returns, Sultan asked him.

721
01:37:14,107 --> 01:37:17,827
Did you kill him, he asked.

722
01:37:18,072 --> 01:37:22,822
He said no. I died, not him.

723
01:37:25,127 --> 01:37:27,817
Sultan asked why.

724
01:37:29,739 --> 01:37:32,379
I got to know this noble man.

725
01:37:32,851 --> 01:37:36,851
He cut me with his...

726
01:37:37,202 --> 01:37:39,742
generosity, with his
friendliness and hospitality.

727
01:37:39,983 --> 01:37:45,183
He cut me with his
sword of goodness, the executioner said.

728
01:37:50,043 --> 01:37:52,053
My Bala.

729
01:37:53,004 --> 01:37:55,074
If you want to get through this...

730
01:37:56,630 --> 01:37:58,990
use the sword of goodness.

731
01:38:54,625 --> 01:38:57,605
You disappointed my father, Nikola.

732
01:38:59,911 --> 01:39:02,771
What I will say now are the words
of my father, not mine.

733
01:39:03,741 --> 01:39:08,641
If I was him, I would make
you a shepherd.

734
01:39:12,086 --> 01:39:15,226
Doing things with Governor Yargucu, huh?

735
01:39:15,554 --> 01:39:18,944
You waste your enemies.

736
01:39:19,231 --> 01:39:23,831
You behave like Mongols'
leading Bey, not the Emperor's!

737
01:39:24,849 --> 01:39:28,849
I do everything to win.

738
01:39:30,426 --> 01:39:34,426
I am surprised that you don't know that
everything can be done to win.

739
01:39:34,542 --> 01:39:39,122
Enough! Don't try to cover your failures.

740
01:39:39,792 --> 01:39:41,492
It's in vain.

741
01:39:42,149 --> 01:39:44,369
You lost Kalanoz and his army.

742
01:39:44,967 --> 01:39:48,057
How long will we tolerate you?

743
01:39:48,617 --> 01:39:51,667
How long will we tolerate you?

744
01:39:52,750 --> 01:39:56,090
Turks are more powerful than before
because of you!

745
01:39:56,669 --> 01:40:01,179
Osman's successes attract Turks.

746
01:40:01,326 --> 01:40:03,486
Osman is getting more powerful.

747
01:40:03,582 --> 01:40:06,842
Even if I am alone...

748
01:40:07,790 --> 01:40:10,180
I will kill Osman.

749
01:40:12,106 --> 01:40:14,136
As for our Emperor...

750
01:40:19,884 --> 01:40:22,734
if he wants to dismiss me...

751
01:40:24,881 --> 01:40:27,181
he can.

752
01:40:27,563 --> 01:40:30,863
I did whatever I could for this to happen.

753
01:40:33,261 --> 01:40:36,641
However, my father wants to
give you one last chance.

754
01:40:39,422 --> 01:40:41,362
Come here.

755
01:40:48,058 --> 01:40:49,548
İznik.

756
01:40:52,241 --> 01:40:54,221
It's important for us.

757
01:40:54,991 --> 01:40:59,911
We shouldn't let Turks get there
like Suleiman ibn Qutalmish did.

758
01:41:00,422 --> 01:41:03,862
We seek help from Crusades to
get Turks out of İznik.

759
01:41:04,893 --> 01:41:08,893
However, this led us to lose
Constantinople.

760
01:41:09,973 --> 01:41:12,673
If we don't take the necessary measures...

761
01:41:13,096 --> 01:41:16,796
we will be in danger.

762
01:41:17,413 --> 01:41:19,863
What is the Emperor's order?

763
01:41:20,098 --> 01:41:24,758
Patrol unions are present through
Bilecik, İnegöl, Yarhisar and İznik.

764
01:41:24,895 --> 01:41:29,375
You will encamp with governors.

765
01:41:31,499 --> 01:41:35,099
Then the governors won't pay
taxes to Seljuq.

766
01:41:41,927 --> 01:41:44,567
What will Geyhatu say about it?

767
01:41:44,733 --> 01:41:47,353
Geyhatu is in the war.

768
01:41:47,501 --> 01:41:51,361
We are sure he won't divide
his army for another war.

769
01:41:53,793 --> 01:41:58,023
This war isn't between me and Osman.

770
01:41:59,791 --> 01:42:03,081
It is between Byzantine and Seljuqs.

771
01:42:05,477 --> 01:42:08,167
What about the army you send me?

772
01:42:08,352 --> 01:42:11,632
Dukas, commander of Trakya unions.

773
01:42:13,928 --> 01:42:16,158
He's on his way.

774
01:42:19,610 --> 01:42:22,670
Dukas is our most skillful commander.

775
01:42:23,774 --> 01:42:27,084
He will support you with his army.

776
01:42:27,894 --> 01:42:29,684
Nikola.

777
01:42:32,822 --> 01:42:36,822
I suggest you forget the
disagreements between each other.

778
01:42:39,019 --> 01:42:40,409
Go now.

779
01:42:40,604 --> 01:42:44,704
Tell everyone to prepare for the big war.

780
01:42:45,027 --> 01:42:48,377
You will prepare them for the war.

781
01:42:48,649 --> 01:42:51,099
Victory, Nikola.

782
01:42:51,477 --> 01:42:55,167
It will make your our powerful commander.

783
01:42:55,235 --> 01:42:59,325
And defeat will not only
disappoint my father...

784
01:42:59,879 --> 01:43:03,389
but also you will
pay for it with your life.

785
01:43:07,695 --> 01:43:10,965
I won't disappoint our Emperor.

786
01:43:11,663 --> 01:43:14,503
Nikola, I hope.

787
01:44:06,835 --> 01:44:09,435
I know why you're sad.

788
01:44:09,519 --> 01:44:11,309
Am I?

789
01:44:11,941 --> 01:44:14,891
Yes.

790
01:44:16,590 --> 01:44:19,580
I know you.
I understand you.

791
01:44:20,825 --> 01:44:23,135
Why am I sad, then?

792
01:44:23,679 --> 01:44:25,659
You tell me.

793
01:44:26,508 --> 01:44:30,508
Say what you want to say, Gonca.

794
01:44:33,493 --> 01:44:37,143
We didn't need her doweries.

795
01:44:37,664 --> 01:44:40,474
We didn't.

796
01:44:44,193 --> 01:44:46,073
Won't you say something?

797
01:44:47,040 --> 01:44:49,910
Osman Bey is okay with it.

798
01:44:52,079 --> 01:44:55,269
We can't say anything.

799
01:44:55,883 --> 01:44:58,803
- However...
- Gonca.

800
01:45:00,211 --> 01:45:01,481
Enough.

801
01:45:16,796 --> 01:45:21,376
We're here for justice.

802
01:45:22,712 --> 01:45:24,892
Don't be shy.

803
01:45:27,165 --> 01:45:31,805
Tell us what happened.

804
01:45:33,998 --> 01:45:37,188
As I said before, I changed my mind.

805
01:45:37,457 --> 01:45:40,167
I decided to sell my property
to Osman Bey.

806
01:45:50,479 --> 01:45:53,229
Don't trick yourself...

807
01:45:54,372 --> 01:45:56,292
as he can't defend himself.

808
01:46:00,039 --> 01:46:05,179
Allah sees you and hears you.

809
01:46:07,445 --> 01:46:09,865
Tell us now.

810
01:46:13,122 --> 01:46:15,822
What happened between you two?

811
01:46:18,845 --> 01:46:21,155
My Bey.

812
01:46:21,737 --> 01:46:23,947
He didn't want to sell
his property that day...

813
01:46:25,062 --> 01:46:27,072
I was so angry.

814
01:46:27,958 --> 01:46:30,938
I took it as an insult to our Bey.

815
01:46:31,921 --> 01:46:35,491
Then I....

816
01:46:35,646 --> 01:46:38,146
forced him to sell his property.

817
01:46:38,722 --> 01:46:40,542
I said I'd beat him...

818
01:46:42,774 --> 01:46:45,564
if he wouldn't sell his property.

819
01:46:51,570 --> 01:46:54,320
Beat him?

820
01:46:58,944 --> 01:47:01,254
Forgive me, my Bey.

821
01:47:05,992 --> 01:47:07,132
Did it happen?

822
01:47:08,885 --> 01:47:10,895
Yes.

823
01:47:16,361 --> 01:47:18,951
We should punish Boran...

824
01:47:19,632 --> 01:47:25,472
as he threatened him and forced him...

825
01:47:26,565 --> 01:47:29,175
to do something.

826
01:47:30,265 --> 01:47:32,605
I have consent, my Sheikh.

827
01:47:37,253 --> 01:47:39,973
You will keep your property.

828
01:47:45,819 --> 01:47:49,819
And he will be given ten golds...

829
01:47:50,498 --> 01:47:54,498
as he was oppressed.

830
01:48:18,968 --> 01:48:22,968
You won't pay taxes to Seljuqs anymore.

831
01:48:23,936 --> 01:48:27,936
I and the Emperor will protect you.

832
01:48:31,760 --> 01:48:34,050
What does the Emperor want from us?

833
01:48:34,481 --> 01:48:39,191
The Emperor wants your blood.

834
01:48:43,213 --> 01:48:47,213
A war will happen soon
and there will be so much blood.

835
01:48:48,019 --> 01:48:53,139
However, with the victory, we will
take our honor and...

836
01:48:54,084 --> 01:48:56,584
our lands that Turks defeated back.

837
01:48:56,669 --> 01:48:58,009
What about the army?

838
01:48:59,958 --> 01:49:02,518
Will the Emperor send an army?

839
01:49:03,103 --> 01:49:05,663
He will.

840
01:49:05,751 --> 01:49:07,901
Who will lead the army?

841
01:49:12,900 --> 01:49:14,180
Dukas.

842
01:49:20,581 --> 01:49:23,821
That's good news, Governor Nikola.

843
01:49:24,620 --> 01:49:28,620
Dukas is a big commander.

844
01:49:29,125 --> 01:49:32,505
It's time to get it from his son.

845
01:49:33,018 --> 01:49:34,938
We are late.

846
01:49:35,197 --> 01:49:37,467
We won't pay taxes to Turks.

847
01:49:37,787 --> 01:49:41,787
And a powerful commander will support us.

848
01:49:43,352 --> 01:49:46,802
Turks are done.

849
01:49:53,207 --> 01:49:54,697
Leo.

850
01:49:56,107 --> 01:49:58,387
Why don't you say anything?

851
01:49:59,177 --> 01:50:01,667
I don't want to be in this war.

852
01:50:04,507 --> 01:50:06,727
Do you hear yourself?

853
01:50:07,138 --> 01:50:11,428
Ending the trade and
making Geyhatu angry...

854
01:50:11,443 --> 01:50:13,653
won't make us any good.

855
01:50:14,372 --> 01:50:18,522
While Turks harm our
soldiers, our lands and our honor...

856
01:50:18,544 --> 01:50:21,594
how can you talk about trade, Leo?

857
01:50:21,638 --> 01:50:24,158
You should be angry towards Turks.

858
01:50:24,463 --> 01:50:28,173
Nikola asked me what do
I think and I answered.

859
01:50:30,053 --> 01:50:33,393
Kepp your thoughts, Leo.

860
01:50:33,706 --> 01:50:38,476
If you don't side with us
and be against our Emperor...

861
01:50:39,285 --> 01:50:43,535
you will be seen as a Turk.

862
01:50:55,262 --> 01:50:56,442
My Bey.

863
01:50:59,692 --> 01:51:02,042
My Bey, it won't happen again.

864
01:51:03,091 --> 01:51:05,391
I have learnt my lesson.

865
01:51:06,047 --> 01:51:08,287
Forgive me.

866
01:51:21,315 --> 01:51:23,575
Your regret and sorrow...

867
01:51:25,094 --> 01:51:27,264
shows that...

868
01:51:28,621 --> 01:51:30,771
you pay for what you do.

869
01:51:33,110 --> 01:51:34,840
As for the golds...

870
01:51:37,783 --> 01:51:39,503
you're my Alp...

871
01:51:42,602 --> 01:51:44,022
I will take care of that.

872
01:51:44,095 --> 01:51:45,565
Osman Bey.

873
01:51:46,613 --> 01:51:47,833
Osman Bey.

874
01:51:49,262 --> 01:51:51,812
Today, I have learned what justice means.

875
01:51:52,948 --> 01:51:57,578
I have seen how a ruler should be.

876
01:52:00,445 --> 01:52:02,325
Please, Osman Bey.

877
01:52:04,669 --> 01:52:06,329
Buy my property.

878
01:52:08,130 --> 01:52:10,670
I want to sell it.

879
01:52:12,428 --> 01:52:14,908
I will be honored if you accept.

880
01:52:19,670 --> 01:52:22,480
Then...

881
01:52:23,242 --> 01:52:26,062
I will pay double.

882
01:52:27,592 --> 01:52:29,332
You're welcome.

883
01:52:29,608 --> 01:52:31,058
You're welcome.

884
01:52:31,270 --> 01:52:32,430
My Bey.

885
01:52:35,601 --> 01:52:37,861
From the governor.

886
01:52:46,196 --> 01:52:47,836
Boran, come on.

887
01:52:58,995 --> 01:53:01,675
You will rise, Osman Bey.

888
01:53:06,539 --> 01:53:07,989
My friend.

889
01:53:08,398 --> 01:53:12,398
If Köprühisar falls, İnegöl
l will be the next.

890
01:53:12,924 --> 01:53:14,904
You know that so well.

891
01:53:15,232 --> 01:53:17,512
We won't let that happen.

892
01:53:21,338 --> 01:53:25,338
I trust you and your soldiers.

893
01:53:27,216 --> 01:53:29,316
What worries me is Leo.

894
01:53:31,109 --> 01:53:33,189
I have known Leo since he was a child.

895
01:53:34,318 --> 01:53:37,338
Persuade him before Dukas comes.

896
01:53:39,182 --> 01:53:40,742
What if I fail?

897
01:53:41,479 --> 01:53:45,479
Then, I'll do what is necessary.

898
01:53:46,840 --> 01:53:49,750
Don't worry, Nikola.

899
01:53:50,921 --> 01:53:53,311
You can trust me.

900
01:53:54,563 --> 01:53:57,583
I trust you, my friend.

901
01:54:21,996 --> 01:54:24,536
Why are you so nervous?

902
01:54:25,464 --> 01:54:29,354
It's good that Dukas
is coming with an army.

903
01:54:30,192 --> 01:54:31,572
Helen.

904
01:54:32,790 --> 01:54:35,020
This is my last opportunity.

905
01:54:36,123 --> 01:54:38,173
If I fail...

906
01:54:38,625 --> 01:54:41,345
the Emperor will kill
me before Osman does.

907
01:54:42,259 --> 01:54:44,719
Dukas is coming for your victory.

908
01:54:44,944 --> 01:54:48,214
A good commander, Dukas, will serve you.

909
01:54:49,448 --> 01:54:54,658
The Emperor won't touch you.

910
01:54:56,570 --> 01:54:58,720
If I lose...

911
01:55:00,362 --> 01:55:02,282
If I lose...

912
01:55:02,961 --> 01:55:06,171
the Emperor will kill me by an
assassinator or...

913
01:55:06,293 --> 01:55:12,033
with poisonous wine.

914
01:55:17,806 --> 01:55:20,316
You can go, Helen.

915
01:55:26,130 --> 01:55:27,370
Helen.

916
01:55:28,668 --> 01:55:31,838
Leo.
Tell them to follow Leo.

917
01:55:32,081 --> 01:55:34,491
I can't just trust Atnos.

918
01:55:35,485 --> 01:55:41,475
Find some spies for us. I
want to learn what he does.

919
01:55:42,935 --> 01:55:45,525
If he doesn't give up on his thoughts...

920
01:55:46,170 --> 01:55:48,940
I will have to kill him.

921
01:56:17,899 --> 01:56:19,239
Osman Bey.

922
01:56:23,747 --> 01:56:27,127
What happened, Governor Leo?
Why are we hiding?

923
01:56:27,365 --> 01:56:29,415
I am being followed.

924
01:56:29,747 --> 01:56:34,517
I even deceived my closest soldiers
and came here.

925
01:56:38,556 --> 01:56:41,326
What is Nikola doing again?

926
01:56:41,678 --> 01:56:46,618
The Emperor sent his son Mikail
to İznik to see Nikola.

927
01:56:50,331 --> 01:56:52,081
Then...

928
01:56:53,752 --> 01:56:55,702
a big war is coming.

929
01:56:57,479 --> 01:56:59,749
It's worse than
a war this time, Osman Bey.

930
01:56:59,791 --> 01:57:03,911
The Emperor ordered that they won't pay
taxes to Seljuqs anymore.

931
01:57:08,647 --> 01:57:10,957
They will fight not only with us...

932
01:57:13,685 --> 01:57:15,675
but also with you.

933
01:57:17,552 --> 01:57:18,692
A new army will come.

934
01:57:18,773 --> 01:57:22,323
Commander Dukas will serve Nikola
with a big army.

935
01:57:26,007 --> 01:57:29,357
- Who is Dukas?
- A brave commander...

936
01:57:29,385 --> 01:57:31,425
from a noble family.

937
01:57:31,697 --> 01:57:36,087
He has big victories.
And he hates Turks so much.

938
01:57:39,024 --> 01:57:43,604
He will form a big line of defense
with the support of governors.

939
01:57:45,097 --> 01:57:49,627
Everyone's life is in danger.
Be careful.

940
01:57:50,390 --> 01:57:52,860
What about the other governors?

941
01:57:53,300 --> 01:57:55,830
Can they take the risk for such a war?

942
01:57:55,900 --> 01:57:58,920
I told Nicola that I don't take sides
in this war.

943
01:57:58,934 --> 01:58:02,054
But the fat is in the fire now.

944
01:58:02,898 --> 01:58:09,328
The other governors can't refuse Nicola
even after all the throttling...

945
01:58:09,425 --> 01:58:11,955
we experienced.

946
01:58:12,245 --> 01:58:16,295
Osman Bey, they don't want to
pay tax to Seljuqs.

947
01:58:17,323 --> 01:58:20,243
This is why they can risk everything.

948
01:58:21,907 --> 01:58:27,227
Kopruhisar's Governor Agnosise is the
best supporter of this war.

949
01:58:27,866 --> 01:58:29,706
He trusts Ducas.

950
01:58:34,040 --> 01:58:35,500
Governor Leo.

951
01:58:37,653 --> 01:58:40,463
This means your life is in danger too.

952
01:58:41,733 --> 01:58:46,603
He can't touch me as I am
coming from the family of Emperor.

953
01:58:47,966 --> 01:58:51,306
But he'll want to get rid of me
in the first chance.

954
01:58:52,763 --> 01:58:54,943
You should know that
you are not alone.

955
01:58:56,268 --> 01:59:02,188
Everybody who stands against the cruelty
is my brother.

956
01:59:04,603 --> 01:59:06,613
You should know that.

957
01:59:22,400 --> 01:59:23,810
Malhun Hatun.

958
01:59:24,788 --> 01:59:27,168
You don't seem well.
Is there anything wrong?

959
01:59:27,212 --> 01:59:28,742
I'm fine.

960
01:59:29,468 --> 01:59:31,278
I'm just a bit weak.

961
01:59:34,717 --> 01:59:36,917
Can I come in Malhun Hatun?

962
01:59:41,378 --> 01:59:43,788
Come Bala Hatun.

963
01:59:50,786 --> 01:59:53,136
Let us be alone.

964
02:00:01,867 --> 02:00:04,647
We have something to talk about.

965
02:00:05,901 --> 02:00:08,251
We don't, Bala Hatun.

966
02:00:09,157 --> 02:00:11,127
It is over.

967
02:00:13,709 --> 02:00:16,139
Won't you stand up?

968
02:00:18,642 --> 02:00:21,722
Don't you see I can't?

969
02:00:24,430 --> 02:00:26,180
Come sit.

970
02:00:28,495 --> 02:00:30,675
I am not here to argue.

971
02:00:32,927 --> 02:00:36,957
As long as you know your limits...

972
02:00:37,300 --> 02:00:39,590
I have no problem with you.

973
02:00:51,451 --> 02:00:53,651
I know my limits, Bala Hatun.

974
02:00:55,320 --> 02:00:58,360
I am a Hatun of this tent.

975
02:01:00,031 --> 02:01:04,511
You were needed to unite
the two tribes.

976
02:01:05,196 --> 02:01:07,196
Nothing else.

977
02:01:10,855 --> 02:01:12,615
What is wrong with you?

978
02:01:12,615 --> 02:01:14,480
You are not fine.

979
02:01:14,480 --> 02:01:16,260
I am fine.

980
02:01:16,928 --> 02:01:18,388
I am alright.

981
02:01:24,728 --> 02:01:26,588
Malhun Hatun!

982
02:01:28,201 --> 02:01:29,811
Malhun Hatun!

983
02:01:29,827 --> 02:01:30,957
Malhun Hatun!

984
02:01:36,158 --> 02:01:37,729
Zoe!

985
02:01:37,729 --> 02:01:39,339
Alaca!

986
02:01:40,136 --> 02:01:42,906
Malhun Hatun!
Malhun Hatun!

987
02:01:43,946 --> 02:01:48,156
If you want to get through this,
use sword of goodness.

988
02:01:53,116 --> 02:01:54,916
Hatuns!

989
02:02:02,376 --> 02:02:03,756
Malhun Hatun!

990
02:02:04,819 --> 02:02:08,299
Hatuns! Bring the healer Hatuns!

991
02:02:09,928 --> 02:02:11,578
Go!

992
02:02:11,679 --> 02:02:12,969
Malhun Hatun!

993
02:02:17,487 --> 02:02:19,097
Malhun Hatun!

994
02:02:22,523 --> 02:02:24,413
Malhun Hatun!

995
02:02:29,117 --> 02:02:32,655
We have valiant alps eyvallah (for sure).

996
02:02:32,655 --> 02:02:35,715
We'll overcome this too, my Bey.

997
02:02:37,390 --> 02:02:39,610
Let's hope for the best.

998
02:02:42,966 --> 02:02:44,866
Eventually...

999
02:02:46,659 --> 02:02:49,229
this will lead us to war.

1000
02:02:50,774 --> 02:02:55,364
However, even if we win...

1001
02:02:57,241 --> 02:03:00,181
we'll not have the same power
as before.

1002
02:03:02,198 --> 02:03:05,758
Both the Emperor and Nicola
are taking risk.

1003
02:03:06,746 --> 02:03:12,226
This war will not be ours.
It'll be Seljuqs'.

1004
02:03:14,448 --> 02:03:16,988
I'll go to Sultan.

1005
02:03:18,548 --> 02:03:21,178
I'll go to Sultan but..

1006
02:03:21,567 --> 02:03:23,857
I don't have much hope.

1007
02:03:24,422 --> 02:03:26,582
Why, my Bey?

1008
02:03:27,110 --> 02:03:30,789
He still has an army even though
he is under Geyhatu's order.

1009
02:03:30,789 --> 02:03:35,165
While everywhere in Anatolia is
full of rebels...

1010
02:03:35,165 --> 02:03:37,795
hoping for an army is just a dream,
Master Davut.

1011
02:03:39,102 --> 02:03:41,972
Even if we lose...

1012
02:03:42,623 --> 02:03:45,146
they cannot exile us from our land
so easily.

1013
02:03:45,146 --> 02:03:48,766
The order is Emperors...

1014
02:03:50,182 --> 02:03:52,892
But the land is ours.

1015
02:03:55,535 --> 02:03:58,695
We'll fight until the last
drop of our blood.

1016
02:03:59,647 --> 02:04:04,897
We prefer dying one thousand times
to give them an inch of land!

1017
02:04:07,400 --> 02:04:11,930
Brother, talk to all of the Beys.

1018
02:04:13,252 --> 02:04:16,842
But don't tell them where
the information is coming from.

1019
02:04:17,475 --> 02:04:21,845
Everybody shall get ready with
their alps for a huge war.

1020
02:04:25,616 --> 02:04:28,106
As you order, Osman Bey.
Excuse me.

1021
02:04:29,041 --> 02:04:30,321
Eyvallah (thank you).

1022
02:04:45,198 --> 02:04:47,238
My Lord...

1023
02:04:49,220 --> 02:04:51,750
give us power.

1024
02:05:02,917 --> 02:05:04,697
- Osman Bey!
- Bala!

1025
02:05:09,169 --> 02:05:12,119
Tell me.
You look pale.

1026
02:05:12,403 --> 02:05:14,323
Malhun Hatun.

1027
02:05:14,936 --> 02:05:17,556
- What happened to Malhun Hatun?
- She is not alright.

1028
02:05:17,577 --> 02:05:21,107
Healer Hatuns are taking care of her.
I summoned the doctor in Sogut.

1029
02:05:21,371 --> 02:05:23,471
What do you mean Bala?

1030
02:05:46,243 --> 02:05:47,963
Malhun Hatun.

1031
02:05:48,210 --> 02:05:49,800
Are you fine.

1032
02:05:50,513 --> 02:05:53,573
I am fine, Osman Bey, don't worry.

1033
02:06:04,186 --> 02:06:05,776
Fine.

1034
02:06:06,316 --> 02:06:08,496
Good, thank Lord.

1035
02:06:11,794 --> 02:06:14,564
- Osman Bey.
- Yes?

1036
02:06:15,240 --> 02:06:17,850
I have an important thing to say.

1037
02:06:20,081 --> 02:06:21,601
What's it?

1038
02:06:27,093 --> 02:06:29,453
Good news, Bey of Kayi.

1039
02:06:31,828 --> 02:06:34,798
You won't yearn for a child anymore.

1040
02:07:03,123 --> 02:07:05,573
What do you mean Malhun Hatun?

1041
02:07:06,959 --> 02:07:11,979
